<!-- FEATURES -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Features</div>
    <h2 id="features-title">Knowledge that finds you</h2>
    <div class="lib-features-grid" role="list">

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Zero-Friction Awareness</h3>
        <p>On every session start, your agent sees a catalog of available skills. It automatically searches for relevant patterns when you're working on security, APIs, databases, testing -- without being asked.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Auto-Research</h3>
        <p>Ask about a topic with no existing skill? The librarian searches the web, pulls from authoritative sources (official docs, RFCs, style guides), and creates a permanent skill. Fewer dead ends.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Quality-Weighted Search</h3>
        <p>BM25 relevance blended with a heuristic quality score &mdash; specificity, examples, actionability, source authority. Sub-section chunking returns precise, focused results, and the best skills rank first.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>{{ versions.librarian.packs }} Community Packs</h3>
        <p>Browse and install curated packs without leaving your editor. Security, API design, Git, TypeScript, Docker, PostgreSQL, testing, and more. Every community contribution is prompt-injection-screened in CI before it can merge.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Ed25519 Integrity</h3>
        <p>Every skill is signed on write &mdash; including ones the agent creates at runtime &mdash; and verified on load. Tampered files are flagged <code>TAMPERED</code>, never served silently. Content guard screens prose for prompt injection while allowing security examples in code blocks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Hardened Network Paths</h3>
        <p>Every fetch rejects private, loopback, and cloud-metadata addresses, pins resolved IPs against DNS rebinding, and re-vets each redirect hop. <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> is scoped to GitHub hosts only. Fetched web content is wrapped in explicit untrusted-data delimiters.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Crash-Safe Installs</h3>
        <p>Pack installs are transactional &mdash; a mid-install failure rolls back instead of destroying existing skills. Progressive disclosure reads through to disk, so an idle server never forgets your skills.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="lib-feature-card" role="listitem">
        <h3>Zero Dependencies</h3>
        <p>Built on Node.js built-ins only. No supply chain risk. No <code>npm install</code>. Web research uses native HTTPS. Fast cold start, small footprint.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TOOLS REFERENCE -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="tools-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Tools Reference</div>
    <h2 id="tools-title">14 MCP tools exposed to your agent</h2>
    <div class="lib-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="MCP tools reference table">
      <table class="lib-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Tool</th>
            <th scope="col">Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>find_and_load</td>
            <td>Search and return the best matching skill in one call. If no skill exists, auto-researches the topic from authoritative web sources and returns content for skill creation. The zero-friction entry point.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>find_skill</td>
            <td>BM25 full-text search across skill names, descriptions, categories, and content. Returns ranked results with scores.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>load_skill</td>
            <td>Load a complete skill by name. Returns content and available section slugs for <code>load_section</code>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>load_section</td>
            <td>Load a specific section within a skill by slug path for focused, minimal context loading.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>list_skills</td>
            <td>List all installed skills with metadata, categories, integrity status, and section slugs.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>browse_packs</td>
            <td>Browse available community skill packs with descriptions and install commands. Searchable by keyword.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>install_pack</td>
            <td>Download, validate, and install a skill pack from the community repo or a direct URL. Deduplicates and re-indexes.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>research_topic</td>
            <td>Search the web, score sources by authority (official docs first), and fetch content from the top results. For building skills from current, authoritative information.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>fetch_page</td>
            <td>Fetch a single URL and extract readable text. Strips HTML, preserves code blocks and headings.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>create_skill</td>
            <td>Validate, save, and index a new skill. Triggers catalog update so the agent immediately knows about it.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>validate_skill</td>
            <td>Check a skill's structure, frontmatter, and content guard compliance without saving.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>export_pack</td>
            <td>Write selected skills to disk as a shareable pack with <code>pack.json</code> manifest.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>skill_status</td>
            <td>Check cryptographic integrity of a single skill. Reports VERIFIED, TAMPERED, or UNSIGNED.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>server_status</td>
            <td>Returns version, skill count, uptime, index stats, and configuration summary.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- SKILL FORMAT -->
<section class="lib-section" aria-labelledby="format-title">
  <div class="lib-wrap">
    <div class="section-label">Skill Format</div>
    <h2 id="format-title">Markdown with YAML frontmatter</h2>
    <p>Skills are plain Markdown files with structured frontmatter. The BM25 index operates at section and sub-section level, so well-structured skills return more precise search results.</p>
    <pre class="lib-pre"><code><span class="code-meta">---</span>
<span class="code-key">name</span>: <span class="code-str">my-skill</span>
<span class="code-key">version</span>: <span class="code-str">1.0.0</span>
<span class="code-key">category</span>: <span class="code-str">[development, patterns]</span>
<span class="code-key">description</span>: <span class="code-str">Brief description for search results</span>
<span class="code-meta">---</span>

<span class="code-cmd">## Section Heading</span>
<span class="code-comment">Content indexed at section level.</span>

<span class="code-cmd">### Sub-Section</span>
<span class="code-comment">Finer-grained content loaded independently via load_section.</span></code></pre>
    <p class="lib-install-note" style="margin-top: 16px;">Sections map directly to <code>load_section</code> calls. The BM25 index scores each chunk independently, so agents get the narrowest useful slice of knowledge rather than an entire document.</p>
  </div>
</section>

